Since the late 20th century, technological advances in lithium batteries—which offer superior energy density and current output versus lead-acid batteries—have revived public interest as zero-emission vehicle options.', 'Which quotation from the text most directly supports the claim that battery advances renewed interest in electric vehicles?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "However, its limited range hindered mass adoption throughout the 20th century."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Since the late 20th century, technological advances in lithium batteries—which offer superior energy density and current output versus lead-acid batteries—have revived public interest as zero-emission vehicle options."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Electricity was among the preferred methods for powering early motor vehicles because it was quieter, provided comfort, and ease of operation."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Internal combustion engines were the dominant propulsion mechanisms for cars and trucks for about 100 years, although electricity-powered locomotion became commonplace in other vehicle types, such as overhead line-powered mass transit vehicles, as well as special purpose vehicles such as mobility scooters."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Electric vehicle", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_vehicle', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M17-CE004', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'Only the correct quotation connects lithium battery advances directly to renewed public interest in electric vehicles.', '{"C": "This sentence explains the early appeal of electric power, not the later revival.", "A": "This sentence explains the obstacle to adoption, not the reason interest returned.", "D": "This sentence describes the dominance of combustion engines rather than a battery-driven revival."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M17-CI005', 'HDSAT-RW-M17-CI005', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Urban sprawl (also known as suburban sprawl or urban encroachment) is defined as "the rapid expansion of the geographic extent of cities and towns, often characterized by low-density residential housing, single-use zoning, and increased reliance on the private automobile for transportation". Urban sprawl has been described as the unrestricted spread over large expanses of land around an urban area of housing, commercial development, and roads, with little concern for very dense urban planning.
Urban sprawl refers to a special form of urbanization, and it relates to the social and environmental consequences associated with such development. In modern times some suburban areas described as "sprawl" have less detached housing and higher density than the nearby core city. Medieval suburbs suffered from the loss of protection of city walls, before the advent of industrial warfare. Sometimes the urban areas described as the most "sprawling" are the most densely populated.
The modern disadvantages and costs of urban sprawl include increased travel time, transport costs, pollution, and destruction of the countryside. The revenue for building and maintaining urban infrastructure in these areas is gained mostly through property and sales taxes.', 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Urban sprawl is a form of dense, mixed-use development that reduces car use."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Urban sprawl benefits cities mainly by lowering infrastructure costs."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Urban sprawl refers only to the growth of medieval suburbs."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Urban sprawl is low-density, automobile-dependent expansion that brings environmental and economic costs."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Urban sprawl", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_sprawl', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M17-CI005', 'D', ARRAY['D']::TEXT[], 'The passage defines sprawl through low density, single-use zoning and car dependence, then lists travel time, transport costs, pollution and countryside destruction among its costs.', '{"A": "The text defines sprawl as low-density with single-use zoning and increased reliance on private automobiles.", "B": "The text lists increased transport costs and pollution among sprawl''s disadvantages.", "C": "Medieval suburbs are one historical example, not the definition of sprawl."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
