The modern disadvantages and costs of urban sprawl include increased travel time, transport costs, pollution, and destruction of the countryside. The revenue for building and maintaining urban infrastructure in these areas is gained mostly through property and sales taxes.', 'Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "It compares the tax policies of two metropolitan areas."}, {"id": "B", "text": "It defines urban sprawl, notes complications in applying the label, and lists its modern disadvantages."}, {"id": "C", "text": "It traces the history of medieval warfare and its effect on cities."}, {"id": "D", "text": "It argues that urban sprawl is beneficial for most residents."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Urban sprawl", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_sprawl', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M17-TS005', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'The text opens with a definition and quoted characterization, observes that some places labeled sprawl are denser than expected, and closes with the modern costs.', '{"C": "Medieval suburbs appear only as a comparison point; the text is not about warfare.", "D": "The text describes sprawl''s costs rather than arguing that it benefits residents.", "A": "Taxes are mentioned as a revenue source, not compared across areas."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M17-CE005', 'HDSAT-RW-M17-CE005', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence (Textual)', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'Urban sprawl (also known as suburban sprawl or urban encroachment) is defined as "the rapid expansion of the geographic extent of cities and towns, often characterized by low-density residential housing, single-use zoning, and increased reliance on the private automobile for transportation". Urban sprawl has been described as the unrestricted spread over large expanses of land around an urban area of housing, commercial development, and roads, with little concern for very dense urban planning.
Urban sprawl refers to a special form of urbanization, and it relates to the social and environmental consequences associated with such development. In modern times some suburban areas described as "sprawl" have less detached housing and higher density than the nearby core city. Medieval suburbs suffered from the loss of protection of city walls, before the advent of industrial warfare. Sometimes the urban areas described as the most "sprawling" are the most densely populated.
The modern disadvantages and costs of urban sprawl include increased travel time, transport costs, pollution, and destruction of the countryside. The revenue for building and maintaining urban infrastructure in these areas is gained mostly through property and sales taxes.', 'Which quotation from the text most directly supports the claim that urban sprawl is associated with environmental harm?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Medieval suburbs suffered from the loss of protection of city walls, before the advent of industrial warfare."}, {"id": "B", "text": "The revenue for building and maintaining urban infrastructure in these areas is gained mostly through property and sales taxes."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Sometimes the urban areas described as the most \"sprawling\" are the most densely populated."}, {"id": "D", "text": "The modern disadvantages and costs of urban sprawl include increased travel time, transport costs, pollution, and destruction of the countryside."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Urban sprawl", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_sprawl', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M17-CE005', 'D', ARRAY['D']::TEXT[], 'The correct quotation names pollution and destruction of the countryside among sprawl''s costs, which directly supports the claim.', '{"A": "This sentence concerns medieval suburbs and city walls, not modern environmental harm.", "C": "This sentence complicates the use of the label rather than describing harm.", "B": "This sentence concerns how infrastructure is funded."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
INSERT INTO public.questions (id, external_id, assessments, section, domain, skill, difficulty, format, stimulus, prompt, choices, figure_metadata, source_id, source_name, license, attribution, is_released_practice_set, status) VALUES ('RW-M17-CI006', 'HDSAT-RW-M17-CI006', ARRAY['SAT', 'PSAT/NMSQT', 'PSAT 10', 'PSAT 8/9']::TEXT[], 'Reading and Writing', 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Medium', 'multiple_choice', 'A zoo (short for zoological garden; also called a zoological park, animal park, or menagerie) is a facility where animals are kept within enclosures for exhibition and often bred for conservation purposes. Zoos vary greatly in size, ranging from small urban enclosures of a few acres to massive open-range and natural-habitat reserves spanning thousands of acres.
The term zoological garden refers to zoology, the study of animals. The term is derived from the Ancient Greek ζῷον, zōion, ''animal'', and the suffix -λογία, -logia, ''study of''. The abbreviation zoo was first used of the London Zoological Gardens, which was opened for scientific study in 1828, and to the public in 1847. The first modern zoo was the Tierpark Hagenbeck by Carl Hagenbeck in Germany. In the United States alone, zoos are visited by over 181 million people annually.
However, animal welfare organizations have expressed criticism of zoos and the conditions in which animals are kept.', 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '[{"id": "A", "text": "Animal welfare groups support zoos without reservation."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Zoos range from small enclosures to large reserves and are criticized over animal welfare despite their conservation role."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Zoos exist only for entertainment and play no role in conservation."}, {"id": "D", "text": "All zoos are large natural-habitat reserves spanning thousands of acres."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'wikipedia-cc-by-sa-4', 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', 'CC BY-SA 4.0', 'Wikipedia, "Zoo", CC BY-SA 4.0, retrieved 2026-11-02. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoo', FALSE, 'active') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET external_id = EXCLUDED.external_id, assessments = EXCLUDED.assessments, section = EXCLUDED.section, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, skill = EXCLUDED.skill, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, format = EXCLUDED.format, stimulus = EXCLUDED.stimulus, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, figure_metadata = EXCLUDED.figure_metadata, source_id = EXCLUDED.source_id, source_name = EXCLUDED.source_name, license = EXCLUDED.license, attribution = EXCLUDED.attribution, is_released_practice_set = EXCLUDED.is_released_practice_set, status = 'active';
INSERT INTO public.question_keys (question_id, correct_answer, acceptable_answers, explanation, distractor_rationales) VALUES ('RW-M17-CI006', 'B', ARRAY['B']::TEXT[], 'The passage defines zoos, describes their range in size and their popularity, and notes that welfare organizations have criticized the conditions in which animals are kept.', '{"D": "The text says zoos range from small urban enclosures of a few acres to reserves spanning thousands of acres.", "C": "The text says animals are often bred for conservation purposes.", "A": "The text says animal welfare organizations have expressed criticism of zoos and the conditions in which animals are kept."}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET correct_answer = EXCLUDED.correct_answer, acceptable_answers = EXCLUDED.acceptable_answers, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, distractor_rationales = EXCLUDED.distractor_rationales;
